    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Exploration of food truck culture in the US. Starting with a brief history of food trucks in America, we examine its origins in the rugged cowboy west to its current state of brightly painted food trucks that serve coca cola braised pork sandwiches.  We look at the evolution of food truck culture in recent years, identifying factors that have contributed to its meteoric rise.  We explore why chefs prefer to go into the food truck business over the brick and mortar restaurant industry, what kinds of success can be achieved with a food truck operation and what factors also lead to failures for food truck entrepreneurs.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
